        "original_id": "9e3b86e3-4e7c-54b5-8500-b15b5d392e27",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Matt O'Dwyer, Curtis Martin, Adrian Murrell, Corey Dillon\n- Organizations: New York Jets\n- Topics: NFL seasons, rushing performance, free agency, career-ending injury\n\nFacts:\n- Matt O'Dwyer blocked for a 1,000-yard rusher in 1996 and 1997, when Adrian Murrell reached that mark.\n- As a free agent in 1998, Curtis Martin joined the New York Jets.\n- Matt O'Dwyer blocked for a 1,000-yard rusher in 1998, when Curtis Martin reached that mark.\n- Matt O'Dwyer blocked for a 1,000-yard rusher from 1999 through 2002, when Corey Dillon reached that mark.\n- Matt O'Dwyer blocked on lines that produced a 1,000-yard rusher in seven of his 10 NFL seasons.\n- Curtis Martin finished his career with the New York Jets in 2006 because of a career-ending knee injury.",
